WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.080
A time-traveling robot cat,&nbsp;
a monster-hunting afterlife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.714
and a city engulfed in bubbles — Netflix has&nbsp;
some serious Anime gems you don't want to miss!

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.760
In a post-apocalyptic future, the remnants&nbsp;
of humanity live inside a labyrinthine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.620
technological city-state and are hunted by&nbsp;
spiderlike robots known as the Safeguard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:25.080
The 2017 anime action film "Blame!" offers&nbsp;
humanity salvation in the form of Killy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:30.480
a black-clad warrior from "below" who rescues&nbsp;
a young girl named Zuru from the Safeguard.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.860
In search of a human being who possesses the&nbsp;
Net Terminal Gene that can control the robots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:39.720
Killy teams up with Zuru and Cibo, a&nbsp;
cyborg who predates the techno-apocalypse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.040
to save Zuru's village. Conceptually dense&nbsp;
and packed with skull-crushing action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.968
"Blame!" earns the exclamation point in its title.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:52.260
"Attack on Titan" director Tetsuro Araki&nbsp;
envisions a transformed Tokyo in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.520
post-apocalyptic remix of "The Little Mermaid."&nbsp;
Five years before the events of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:01.860
mysterious bubbles began falling from the sky,&nbsp;
triggering strange gravitational abnormalities.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.540
Now, with the entire city of Tokyo encased&nbsp;
in an enormous bubble, teams of surviving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.580
teenagers battle for supplies via dangerous&nbsp;
parkour games. When one game knocks a young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:17.640
Blue Blazes team member named Hibiki to the sea,&nbsp;
a strange girl called Uta manifests out of bubbles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:23.040
to rescue him. Who is Uta? Where did she come&nbsp;
from? And what forgotten secret binds her and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.515
Hibiki together? "Bubble" explores these questions&nbsp;
with skillful writing and eye-popping animation.

00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:30.279
"Beautiful."

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.980
Athletic sixth-grader Kanna has lost&nbsp;
her passion for running after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.980
traumatic death of her mother. But&nbsp;
on the day of the school marathon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:43.080
Kanna wears her mother's bracelet and discovers&nbsp;
its mystical ability to slow time to a crawl.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:48.120
As it turns out, Kanna's running ability is part&nbsp;
of a magical birthright. Accompanied by a talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:53.340
rabbit and a fleet-footed demon boy, she must&nbsp;
hurry across Japan and gather offerings for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:58.260
special feast for deities before time runs out.&nbsp;
Populated by likable characters and visually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.300
appealing gods, "Child of Kamiari Month"&nbsp;
is a clever and absorbing fantasy travelog.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.700
Man's relationship to the environment has been&nbsp;
a powerful theme in anime for a long time. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.080
"Children of the Sea," a young girl named Ruka&nbsp;
discovers her profound connection to the ocean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:18.480
when she meets Umi and Sora, brothers raised&nbsp;
underwater with supernatural aquatic abilities.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.040
As Ruka tries to understand this connection,&nbsp;
she is submerged into a mystery about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.580
disappearing sea life. "Children of&nbsp;
the Sea" engulfs its audience with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:31.116
psychedelic visuals and profound questions&nbsp;
about man's place in the natural world.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:37.200
Sixth-graders Kosuke and Natsume were drifting&nbsp;
apart, but now they are "Drifting Home."

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.560
"See? We'll never do it unless&nbsp;
we cooperate, you little idiot."

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.279
"Quite acting like my sister,&nbsp;
because you're not my sister."

00:02:43.279 --> 00:02:46.740
"I'm glad I'm not because you're a brat!"
When the old, abandoned apartment building they

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:50.640
grew up in faces demolition, the former&nbsp;
best friends reconnect on top of the roof.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:55.980
This all-ages adventure takes on a survivalist&nbsp;
spin when a flash flood suddenly sends the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.660
apartment building adrift in a mysterious,&nbsp;
seemingly endless sea, separating Kosuke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:05.220
Natsume, and their friends from the rest of&nbsp;
the world. The children will have to rely on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.240
their wits if they're going to make it home.&nbsp;
Luckily, they have help in the form of Noppo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.600
the ghost haunting the apartment&nbsp;
building. "Drifting Home" is a smart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.143
satisfying, and occasionally&nbsp;
surreal coming-of-age story.

00:03:16.143 --> 00:03:21.480
"Neon Genesis Evangelion" is a genre-smashing&nbsp;
classic and one of the defining shows of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:27.180
1990s, not just for mecha anime but for the medium&nbsp;
itself. The story follows a 14-year-old boy who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:32.640
reluctantly pilots the giant robot Evangelion&nbsp;
Unit-01 against invading interdimensional beings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.020
called Angels. "Evangelion" was revolutionary&nbsp;
in its combination of thrilling action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.520
striking visuals, and a story that turned&nbsp;
its young heroes' psyches into battlefields.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:46.800
"The End of Evangelion" is, as the title promises,&nbsp;
the conclusion to the original "Evangelion" TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:51.840
series. The last Angel has been destroyed,&nbsp;
leaving the Eva pilots –- despondent Shinji,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:57.960
hotheaded Asuka, and enigmatic Rei –- to face&nbsp;
one final enemy: humanity. Visceral, shocking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:01.680
and brilliant, the end of "The End of&nbsp;
Evangelion" is still discussed today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.734
cementing its place as a modern anime classic.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:09.259
"I'm sure I'll just realize&nbsp;
the obvious, over and over."

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:14.220
"Fireworks" puts an imaginative spin on&nbsp;
a story about a young boy's first love.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:19.020
Norimichi secretly loves his classmate&nbsp;
Nazuna, a beautiful but troubled girl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:22.560
planning to run away from home. On the&nbsp;
day of their town's fireworks festival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.480
Norimichi is helpless to stop Nazuna's&nbsp;
mother from forcibly taking her back home.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.740
Upset and heartbroken, Norimichi&nbsp;
throws a glass marble belonging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.460
to Nazuna and wishes that he could&nbsp;
turn back time. To his surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:40.020
the marble creates an alternate timeline&nbsp;
where Nazuna and Norimichi run away together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:44.220
but how many wishes and alternate worlds&nbsp;
will it take for the star-crossed couple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:49.200
to finally escape their pursuers? Tender and&nbsp;
thoughtful, "Fireworks" is highly invested in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.414
the dreams and fears of its young protagonists,&nbsp;
leading to an emotionally explosive finale.

00:04:54.414 --> 00:04:59.940
High school student Masaru Kato is on his way home&nbsp;
for his little brother's birthday when a random&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:05.580
attacker stabs him in the subway. Kato should be&nbsp;
dead, but instead of the afterlife, he wakes up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:11.040
an austere white room containing several strangers&nbsp;
and a mysterious black sphere called Gantz.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:16.260
After outfitting Kato with a special suit and&nbsp;
futuristic weapons, Gantz orders this team to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:20.100
hunt down monsters invading the city. If&nbsp;
they win, they can regain their freedom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:24.960
but if they fail, the entire team will&nbsp;
die. Bursting with unconventional heroes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:29.220
and hideous monsters, "Gantz: O" is&nbsp;
a relentlessly paced action-thriller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.895
that gives viewers a taste of the&nbsp;
ultra-violent "Gantz" franchise.

00:05:32.895 --> 00:05:36.600
"Watch me! I'm gonna hit&nbsp;
a bullseye on that thing!"

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:41.280
In the near future, giant monsters overrun the&nbsp;
Earth, and humanity's only chance for survival&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:46.440
is to flee the planet with help from alien&nbsp;
technology. 20,000 years later, humans return&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:51.000
to find the Earth's environment transformed&nbsp;
into a world that now belongs to Godzilla.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:55.500
Kaiju fans who can't get enough of the King of&nbsp;
the Monsters should seek out "Godzilla: Planet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:00.540
of the Monsters," the first computer-animated&nbsp;
film in the franchise's history. The far-flung&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:04.680
future setting puts a unique spin on a&nbsp;
classic formula, and without the confines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:09.456
of live action film making, Godzilla is a more&nbsp;
terrifying force of nature than ever before.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:14.760
A young boy takes a fantastical climb&nbsp;
up his family tree in "Mirai," a sweet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:18.420
and profound film by acclaimed&nbsp;
"Belle" director Mamoru Hosoda.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:23.880
4-year-old Kun is upset by the sudden presence&nbsp;
of his new baby sister Mirai and throws tantrums&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:28.980
around his parents. A teenage girl then appears,&nbsp;
telling Kun she is Mirai from the future. Kun goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:33.060
on a magical journey through his family's past,&nbsp;
gaining a better understanding of his parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:38.100
sister, and himself. In 2019, "Mirai" was&nbsp;
nominated for best animated feature at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:43.233
Academy Awards, becoming the first non-Studio&nbsp;
Ghibli anime film to earn the distinction.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:47.580
Anime fans can explore the legendary&nbsp;
giant robot franchise from the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:51.840
beginning with "Mobile Suit Gundam I."&nbsp;
The first of three compilation films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.620
retell the events of the original&nbsp;
1979 anime television series.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:59.940
"Mobile Suit Gundam" introduces Amuro&nbsp;
Ray, a young, burgeoning psychic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:04.260
also known as a "Newtype," and pilot for&nbsp;
the experimental mobile suit weapon known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:09.240
as the Gundam. Engaged in an intergalactic&nbsp;
war, Amuro fights to defend his friends and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:14.520
allies and forms a lifelong rivalry with&nbsp;
the enigmatic, masked pilot Char Aznable.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:17.220
"Mobile Suit Gundam I" and its two companion films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:20.340
are essential viewing for any&nbsp;
mecha anime fan. To see them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:25.323
is to understand why the "Gundam" franchise&nbsp;
has captivated audiences for over 40 years.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:31.260
Energetic young ninja Naruto Uzumaki trains so&nbsp;
that he can one day become leader of his village,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:35.940
but his trust in his teacher is tested in&nbsp;
"Naruto Shippuden the Movie: The Will of Fire."

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:40.800
A celebratory film for the "Naruto" series'&nbsp;
tenth anniversary, "The Will of Fire" follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:45.900
Naruto's pursuit of their teacher, Kakashi,&nbsp;
after he deserts their village. In actuality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:51.420
an evil ninja has cursed Kakashi so that he may&nbsp;
absorb his power, and Naruto is determined to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:55.560
save his mentor before he can sacrifice&nbsp;
himself. "Naruto Shippuden the Movie:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:59.460
The Will of Fire" combines the fluid,&nbsp;
fast-paced action the series is known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:03.654
for with an encouraging story about&nbsp;
overcoming seemingly impossible odds.

00:08:03.654 --> 00:08:07.560
"We have to protect the Leaf Village&nbsp;
I love. That's the only future that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:09.900
matters! That's the future the children need!"

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:15.540
Recently orphaned in a car accident, young Okko&nbsp;
moves into the inn operated by her grandmother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:20.220
and prepares to become its new caretaker. The&nbsp;
inn rejects no one according to her grandmother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:24.600
which is lucky for Okko because she can see&nbsp;
and communicate with the ghosts haunting it.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:28.740
"Okko's Inn" is a cheeky collection of&nbsp;
spirited vignettes. It touches on death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:32.520
openly and gently, with the spirits&nbsp;
helping Okko come to terms with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:36.477
grief as they all prepare to move on&nbsp;
to the next stage of their existence.

00:08:36.909 --> 00:08:41.220
"One Piece" is an international pop&nbsp;
culture phenomenon. The original manga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:46.620
series has over 490 million copies in print,&nbsp;
shattering world records, and the official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:52.560
anime adaptation has aired over 1,000 episodes&nbsp;
since 1999. The sheer immensity of "One Piece"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:57.180
may seem intimidating for viewers eager to&nbsp;
dive into the adventures of Monkey D. Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:01.800
a boy pirate whose body gained the elasticity&nbsp;
of rubber after eating a devil fruit.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:05.520
One place to start? "One Piece:&nbsp;
Strong World," a feature-length&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:09.720
film with an original story developed&nbsp;
by "One Piece" creator Eiichiro Oda.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:15.300
In "Strong World," Luffy and the Straw Hat pirates&nbsp;
are scattered after the evil Shiki, who also has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:20.460
devil fruit power, abducts their navigator Nami=.&nbsp;
Showcasing Oda's eye-catching character designs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:25.300
and spry storytelling, "One Piece: Strong&nbsp;
World" is a buoyant and exciting adventure.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:31.140
The ultimate magical girl, the sailor-suited hero&nbsp;
who fights for love and justice, shines on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:35.700
screen in "Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon Eternal&nbsp;
the Movie." Split into two films on Netflix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:41.340
this faithful adaptation of Naoko Takeuchi's&nbsp;
beloved manga series chronicles Sailor Moon's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:46.080
battles against the Dead Moon Circus. Released&nbsp;
during a solar eclipse, these colorful minions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:51.480
of the wicked Queen Nehelenia threaten everything&nbsp;
Sailor Moon and the Sailor Guardians hold dear.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:56.580
But a mysterious Pegasus named Helios,&nbsp;
who appears in Sailor Chibi Moon's dreams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.580 --> 00:10:00.300
may hold the key to their salvation.&nbsp;
"Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon Eternal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:04.200
the Movie" has it all — friendship,&nbsp;
adventure, talking cats, evil queens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:09.139
circus girls from space, flying dream&nbsp;
horses, and, yes, love and justice.

00:10:09.139 --> 00:10:13.080
What would you do if you could go back in&nbsp;
time to meet your great-great-grandparents?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:16.620
Would you tell them about the future?&nbsp;
Ask them about their past? Or give them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:21.420
a robotic cat from the 22nd century to help&nbsp;
them straighten out their disastrous lives?

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:26.340
The touching and imaginative family film&nbsp;
"Stand by Me Doraemon" chooses the third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:30.960
option. Fifth-grader Nobi is bullied at school&nbsp;
and in danger of failing his classes when he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:36.060
visited by his future descendant and gifted&nbsp;
with a talking robot cat named Doraemon. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:40.560
the help of Doraemon and his endless array of&nbsp;
gadgets, Nobi has the power to give himself a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:44.851
better future. But if he succeeds, will&nbsp;
his new best friend leave him forever?

00:10:44.851 --> 00:10:48.480
What is the strangest thing you've ever&nbsp;
done for love? Whatever your answer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:54.840
middle-schooler Miyo Sasaki has it beat. Miyo's&nbsp;
outgoing personality hides a broken heart. Her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.840 --> 00:11:00.000
father has recently remarried, and her crush,&nbsp;
Hinode, is totally unresponsive to her feelings.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.700
Thanks to a mysterious mask seller, Miyo acquires&nbsp;
a mask that turns her into a cat whenever she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:11.160
wears it. Posing as a stray cat named Taro, Miyo&nbsp;
can forget her troubles and even win Hinode's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:17.172
affections. However, every gift has a price, and&nbsp;
Miyo risks being trapped in her cat form forever.

00:11:18.234 --> 00:11:19.974
"I am in trouble."

00:11:19.974 --> 00:11:24.900
Under its magical trappings, "A Whisker Away"&nbsp;
is a sweet and genuine love story that takes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:29.640
complex emotions of its young heroine seriously&nbsp;
— even when she's an adorable white kitten.

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:34.260
"Words Bubble Up Like Soda Pop" is&nbsp;
a movie as bubbly and effervescent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:37.020
as its title. Cherry is an introverted teenager&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:41.640
who works with senior citizens and prefers&nbsp;
to express himself via handwritten haikus.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:47.040
Smile is a popular streamer and online influencer&nbsp;
who self-consciously hides her braces behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:51.900
a facemask. After a mix-up at a local mall,&nbsp;
their fates are intertwined for a glorious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:57.840
shining summer. Every frame of Kyohei Ishiguro's&nbsp;
sweet romcom pops with vibrancy and color,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:02.496
resulting in a viewing experience so&nbsp;
joyful the screen practically glows.

